From a2887add586c05300ac869e70fef713549a71c81 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StefanVonRanda <16295563+StefanVonRanda@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 08:58:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Add instruction editing with reference images
 (--reference)

MOSS Image Edit (chinoll/Moss-Image-Edit, akhaliq/MOSS-Image-Edit-HQ) is a
LoRA plus an inference contract: the reference images' VAE latents join the
sequence at timestep 0, reference queries attend only to references, and
target and text attend to everything. moss-mlx had no way to feed it
reference images.

- dit.py: reference_cache() runs the references through every block once
  (modulation at t=0, RoPE (index + 1, 0, h, w)) and keeps each block's
  rotated K/V; the target/text pass appends them to its own keys. Valid for
  every step and both CFG branches since references depend on nothing else.
- pipeline.py: Request.references / reference_size; references are scaled
  to fit reference_size with sides snapped to 16 px, no crop, as the
  upstream code prepares them. Turbo rejects references (its student was
  not trained with them).
- cli.py: --reference (repeatable), --reference-size.
The adapter's bare layers.N keys load through the LoRA key-format commit.

Checked: tests/test_edit.py compares the cached path against the edit
written out as one masked [target, text, reference] sequence (max diff
< 1e-4, fp32 toy model); pytest 39 passed. Real run on 0.2.0, compact tier,
--batch with the app's "references" field, 8-step DMD + chinoll's
adapter_model.safetensors, CFG 1, 1024^2: "Change her dress to a red
leather jacket and blue jeans" on the Lisbon street kept scene, pose and
style and added the red jacket (jeans only at the hem; the dress stays);
50 s denoise, 11.1 GB MLX peak.
Not checked: the 28-50 step CFG 4 setting the adapter was trained with,
multiple references, the --precise path on real weights.
